    [BugFix] Mark DeepSeek V4.1 input embeddings dynamic for torch.compile (#18191)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Add `inputs_embeds: 0` to the existing `DeepseekV41Model` torch.compile
    dynamic argument mapping.
    
    MRV2 can pass precomputed embeddings to the backbone. Their token
    dimension varies between profiling, prefill and decode. Marking only
    input_ids and positions dynamic leaves the embedding row count
    specialized, which can cause shape failures when a later invocation has
    a different token count.
    
    The production change is one line. The regression test invokes the real
    decorator with two token counts and checks its dynamic-dimension
    annotations before compilation, without loading model weights.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Fixes compilation with precomputed DeepSeek V4.1 embeddings. No new
    configuration or default changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - On this latest-main-based source: `python -m pytest -q
    tests/ut/models/test_deepseek_v41_compile.py`: 2 passed.
    - Negative control: removing only the inputs_embeds mapping makes both
    cases fail.
    - `bash format.sh ci`: passed with the local actionlint hook excluded;
    no CI configuration changes are included.
    - The same decorator fix was also validated on an A5 950DT MRV2 1P1D
    integration branch using default graph sizes and static kernel disabled:
    512/512 performance requests and 9/9 smoke requests succeeded. In the
    second paired 4K-input/1K-output, concurrency-128 round, output
    throughput was 10668.93 versus 10689.42 tokens/s (about -0.19%). This is
    integration-branch evidence, not an end-to-end validation of this latest
    main checkout.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Signed-off-by: linfeng-yuan <1102311262@qq.com>

